Well, everybody writes here to sob about how extremely unlycky they are, so I
thought I might report this extremely lucky event:

Playing a Barbarian (this is a hack-n-slash game after all) I was doing quite
well and on dlvl 8 aprox, I found this lawful altar and also a white unicorn
and said to myself "hmm, didn't someone post on r.g.h warning about sacrifying
a white unicorn on a lawful altar. Or maybe hid didn't warn, but said it
was good. Now, how was it?". I couldn't decide what had been said, so I
decided to try it out all by myself. And guess what happened...

- minor spoiler follows -



















I was punished. Tough luck, I just hate dragging around that F***ING iron
ball. But just as I notice the ball, I notice a littel 'r' in the room.
And yes! T'was indeed a rock mole, and less than five turns later he had
eaten my chain and parted me from my troubles. This is of course one of
the most basic ways to get rid of the ball, but I've never used it before
anyway. Really pleasing!

Anyway, here's the bug report: although I was released from the ball I
was still Overtaxed. I had to drop all my things and then pick them up again
to lose the extra weight of the non-attached ball.
